y","p_yest":"The high of <strong>43\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 50\u00b0F, and the record is 76\u00b0F (1989). The low of <strong>27\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Moline is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Moline's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Moline has set <strong>48 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 64 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">101 record highs</strong>, far more than the 64 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (77). Moline's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on July 14, 1936.","t_chg":"Moline's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 152 complete years: Moline's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.09 to +0.04) that includes zero. Moline's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.29), about +3.4\u00b0F since 1874.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; September and October fell. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Moline has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Moline's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.22 to +0.72), about +7.2 inches since 1872. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1973 (56.36 in); the driest, 1901 (17.33 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}